---
import ServicePage from '../../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { pairs } from '../../i18n/ui';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Do I have to remember the whole dream?',
    a: 'No. Fragments are often enough. What matters more than completeness is the feeling you woke up with.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does it take?',
    a: 'I take my time over every interpretation. I will tell you when you can expect yours as soon as your dream reaches me.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is this therapy?',
    a: 'No. Dream interpretation is a reflective service, not medical, psychotherapeutic or psychological advice. The details are in the <a href="/agb">AGB § 2a</a>, which is in German.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to my dream?',
    a: 'It stays between us. I do not publish what people entrust to me. The example on this site is my own dream.',
  },
];
---

<ServicePage
  title="Personal Dream Interpretation, Aisling Method"
  description="Personal dream interpretation with the Aisling Method. A detailed written interpretation of your dream, tied to your own situation. 29 € instead of 69 €."
  path="/en/personal-dream-interpretation"
  alternates={pairs.personal}
  lang="en"
  h1="Personal dream interpretation"
  lead="Your dream, read alongside your life. Not looked up, but written for you."
  serviceName="Personal dream interpretation with the Aisling Method"
  faq={faq}>

  <h2>What "personal" means here</h2>
  <p>
    Most answers to dream questions are built for everyone. You look up
    "water" and get the same paragraph as ten thousand other people. As a
    starting point that is not bad. It just rarely fits your dream, because it
    cannot know your situation.
  </p>
  <p>
    A personal dream interpretation goes the other way. I read your dream as
    what it is: a story with an order, a mood, and a particular moment at which
    it came to you. The same dream can mean something different for someone who
    is moving house than for someone waiting on a diagnosis. That is why I
    always ask about your situation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Said plainly: I do work with a symbol book. The Aisling Method has over
    3,000 entries drawn from three decades of practice. The difference is not
    whether symbol knowledge is involved, but what happens with it afterwards.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <p>
    A written document of five to ten pages, as a finished PDF. No chat
    history, no general symbol table. Inside you will find:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your dream in your own words, with the context it came out of</li>
    <li>The core theme: what this dream is actually about</li>
    <li>The I AM and I SHOULD formula, written from your own perspective</li>
    <li>A line by line interpretation, without jargon</li>
    <li>Symbols, colours, places and numbers, and what the tradition sees in them</li>
    <li>A closing reflection and concrete next steps</li>
    <li>Connections to earlier dreams, once I have more than one from you</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can read what that looks like rather than take my word for it:
    <a href="/en/example-interpretation">a full interpretation, start to finish</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>You get in touch</strong> on WhatsApp or by email and tell me briefly what this is about. Not the whole dream yet.</li>
    <li><strong>We sort out the process</strong> and you pay the introductory price through a secure payment link.</li>
    <li><strong>You send your dream</strong>, with a title and as much context about your life as you want to give.</li>
    <li><strong>You receive your interpretation</strong> in writing, written unhurried.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Who this suits</h2>
  <p>
    You, if a dream will not let go. Especially the one that keeps coming back,
    or the one you woke from knowing it mattered. Also if you have already
    looked things up and the answer did not feel right.
  </p>
  <p>
    I work in English and German, for clients in Germany, Austria and
    Switzerland.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>29 € instead of 69 €</strong> as an introductory offer. As a small
    business under §19 UStG, no VAT is charged. If the price does not work
    right now, just write to me. This work should never fail for anyone over
    money.
  </p>

</ServicePage>
